 {
  "name": "over_alpha_general",
  "file": "over_alpha_general.png",
  "writer": "hand-assembled",
  "notes": "real source-over arithmetic: an alpha ramp over an opaque backdrop, then 254 at alpha 128 over an opaque black patch, then a full-canvas 25% white wash. That middle blend is (128*254 + 127*0)/255 = 127.498, only 0.002 from a rounding boundary, so this is the one fixture the exactness gate refuses and the one that carries a tolerance; Pillow composites APNG_BLEND_OP_OVER as a straight lerp that also lerps alpha, so it disagrees with the specification wherever a source pixel is partly transparent",
  "sha256": "0d951e98cf59a215",
